#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:1
#: 5b1c1a2464e443e8a52d1de6d66d4365
msgid "Efficiency, Productivity, and Profitability"
msgstr "效率、生产率与盈利能力"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:3
#: 68834a1f9c9e409c9b656cd774ec4452
msgid ""
"A hospital board is told that North could have met its treatment commitments"
" with fewer resources, East delivered the most care per unit of resource, "
"Central's productivity improved most over the last year, and West obtained "
"the largest increase in revenue per dollar of expenditure. South, meanwhile,"
" reduced avoidable harm while preserving access. The chair asks a natural "
"question: *which hospital performed best?*"
msgstr "某医院集团的董事会听到如下汇报：北院用更少资源也能完成诊疗承诺；东院每单位资源提供的医疗服务最多；中院过去一年的生产率改善最大；西院每投入一元支出所获得的收益增幅最高；与此同时，南院在维持医疗可及性的同时减少了可避免伤害。董事长自然会问：*哪家医院表现最好？*"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:10
#: 27623f685f98451aa7f438a8d5e389b8
msgid ""
"There is no defensible answer until the board says what it means by "
"performance. The five statements use different information and address "
"different responsibilities. North is judged against feasible operating "
"alternatives at one point in time. East is described by an aggregate "
"quantity ratio. Central is compared with itself across periods. West's "
"comparison values quantities at prices. South is evaluated against a "
"production model in which desirable care and undesirable harm arise jointly."
" None of these statements is merely another name for the same ranking."
msgstr "在董事会明确“绩效”究竟指什么之前，这个问题没有可辩护的答案。五项陈述使用不同信息、对应不同责任。北院相对于某一时点的可行经营方案接受评价；东院由一个总量比率描述；中院跨期与自身比较；西院的比较用价格评价数量；南院则置于合意医疗服务与非合意伤害联合产生的生产模型中。它们不是同一种排名的不同名称。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: db6ef31b3ce44afc890cd811ab134f16
msgid "Performance concept"
msgstr "绩效概念"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 2c6e1ae6a8a24b94b42594eb6bad69b2
msgid "Decision question"
msgstr "决策问题"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 71dbb0fea83a40f7afca24b2cf1d3627
msgid "Information that gives the answer meaning"
msgstr "使答案具有意义的信息"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: ef6247ced25c45399b5ed9aed9db50b3
msgid "Technical efficiency"
msgstr "技术效率"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 616e2b885a3c4a85a7609266c83d636a
msgid ""
"Could the organization preserve its service commitment with fewer "
"controllable resources, or deliver more with its current resource budget?"
msgstr "组织能否在履行服务承诺的同时减少可控资源，或用当前资源预算提供更多服务？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 88a205406d9843bb9d0d510d516906a1
msgid ""
"A production technology, a credible comparison population, and a clear "
"statement of which quantities management can change"
msgstr "一项生产技术、可信的比较总体，以及对管理者可以改变哪些数量的清晰说明"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: cb50c5ee2e6d4756844142cf3e1dfa14
msgid "Productivity level"
msgstr "生产率水平"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: ba962f74ca594d24a2f1d391bc274c4d
msgid ""
"How much aggregate output is being delivered per unit of aggregate input at "
"this time?"
msgstr "当前每单位总投入提供了多少总产出？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 0c39b2f2013a4acab90df9a133901d25
msgid "An explicit rule for aggregating heterogeneous quantities"
msgstr "一项明确的异质数量聚合规则"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 45a95845637e403c8199842a468f49e3
msgid "Productivity change"
msgstr "生产率变化"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 953fb5c15b0646d08f5d2a9b101cdb8f
msgid ""
"Has aggregate output quantity changed more favorably than aggregate input "
"quantity between two periods?"
msgstr "两个时期之间，总产出数量是否比总投入数量发生了更有利的变化？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 5bb3695acf544442bbc3595ca87cd709
msgid ""
"Comparable quantity definitions across time and a stated temporal reference "
"policy"
msgstr "跨期可比的数量定义与明确的时间参照政策"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: fd88655f099a4df5bdfb5d2a1acafabd
msgid "Profitability and price recovery"
msgstr "盈利能力与相对价格回收"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 8f780f4341354169b1573ec12ad4b17d
msgid ""
"What financial return do the quantities generate, and how much of its change"
" reflects relative output and input prices?"
msgstr "这些数量带来多少财务回报？回报变化中有多少反映产出价格相对于投入价格的变动？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 0892dc470fa64ca1b6908157f7c6396a
msgid "Observed prices or another explicit valuation system"
msgstr "观测价格或另一套明确的价值评价体系"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: cce34639ba1242bab000453502c890b7
msgid "Environmental performance"
msgstr "环境绩效"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 7d6b2ab248344b49a1c6c8e831691f55
msgid ""
"What useful production and reduction in undesirable outcomes are attainable "
"together?"
msgstr "合意生产与非合意结果削减能够共同实现到什么程度？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md
#: 15d72ef004f246338aa1726580a480e2
msgid ""
"A joint-production model, disposal assumptions, and an improvement programme"
" specified in advance"
msgstr "联合生产模型、处置假设，以及预先设定的改进方案"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:26
#: a10589a3e82a455e897fc306278c9f82
msgid ""
"This separation is not terminology for its own sake. A hospital may be "
"technically efficient because no comparable hospital demonstrates a feasible"
" resource saving at its scale, yet have a lower productivity level because "
"its mandated service mix is resource intensive. Productivity may grow while "
"profitability falls if input prices rise faster than output prices. "
"Emissions may fall because production contracted, not because environmental "
"performance improved. A ranking that mixes these conclusions would hide the "
"policy question rather than answer it."
msgstr "作出这些区分不是在玩术语游戏。一家医院可能在技术上有效率，因为同等规模的可比医院没有展示可行的资源节约；但由于其法定服务组合消耗较多资源，它的生产率水平仍可能较低。如果投入价格涨得比产出价格快，生产率可以上升，盈利能力却会下降。排放减少可能只是因为生产收缩，而非环境绩效改善。把这些结论混成一个排名，会掩盖政策问题，而不是回答它。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:34
#: 05fbe654c60343b5a61a27abad3cd959
msgid ""
"Before calculating anything, a useful performance question therefore names "
"three things: the commitment to be protected, the resources or outcomes that"
" the responsible manager can change over the stated horizon, and the "
"comparison evidence accepted as a feasible alternative. Prices, "
"environmental burdens, and time enter only when the question requires them."
msgstr "因此，在计算之前，一个有用的绩效问题应先说明三件事：必须保护的承诺、责任管理者在给定期限内可以改变的资源或结果，以及被接受为可行替代方案的比较证据。只有当问题需要时，才引入价格、环境负担和时间。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:40
#: c22275f1bd574e1998aa62f122964ace
msgid ""
"Four operating plans compared separately by technical efficiency, an "
"explicitly equal-count service-throughput measure, and observed revenue per "
"unit of cost"
msgstr "分别按技术效率、明确的等权服务产出测度和单位观测成本收益比较四项经营方案"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:45
#: 361bd8bf88f544e9adfc44d152b7e81d
msgid ""
"One dataset, three performance questions. A and B both attain the best "
"input-oriented VRS radial score. Under the deliberately simple rule that "
"counts a standard and a premium service equally, A records greater observed "
"physical productivity. At the supplied prices, B's service mix produces "
"greater revenue per unit of cost and greater observed profit. The three "
"columns answer different questions; they are not interchangeable score "
"scales or causal evaluations of management."
msgstr ""
"一组数据，三个绩效问题。A 与 B 的投入导向 VRS 径向得分都达到最佳。按照一个有意简化、对普通服务与优质服务等权计数的规则，A "
"的观测实物生产率更高；按给定价格，B "
"的服务组合每单位成本带来更多收益，观测利润也更高。三列回答不同问题，不能互换为同一种得分尺度，也不是对管理的因果评价。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:53
#: 0be347488a264a35be7d2671303676c7
msgid ""
"Read the figure across the columns, not down a league table. The first "
"column asks whether a feasible benchmark supports further common resource "
"saving. The second uses a stated equal-count rule to describe service "
"throughput. The third values the observed mix of standard and premium "
"services. A and B exchange places only when the question and measurement "
"scale change. The figure contains no temporal comparison and no undesirable "
"outcome, so it cannot support a conclusion about productivity change or "
"environmental performance."
msgstr ""
"阅读该图时，应横向比较各列，而不是纵向寻找排行榜。第一列询问可行标杆是否支持进一步按共同尺度节约资源；第二列使用明确的等权计数规则描述服务产出；第三列评价普通服务与优质服务的观测组合。A"
" 与 B 只有在问题和测量尺度改变时才交换位置。图中没有时间比较，也没有非合意结果，因而不能支持关于生产率变化或环境绩效的结论。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:61
#: fb68a934a4e44b0891df8936c1c57d4d
msgid ""
"In the opening figure, data envelopment analysis (DEA) supplies the first "
"comparison. It constructs an empirical production comparison for "
"organizations that use multiple resources to deliver multiple products, "
"services, or outcomes, without imposing a parametric functional form in "
"advance. Later frontier-based methods use the same production logic in "
"productivity and environmental analyses. In every case, the optimization "
"takes its meaning from the economics supplied to it: who is responsible for "
"which quantities, what must be preserved, and which operating practices are "
"credible evidence of what could be done."
msgstr ""
"在开篇图中，数据包络分析（data envelopment "
"analysis，DEA）提供第一项比较。它不预先施加参数化函数形式，而是为使用多种资源提供多种产品、服务或结果的组织构造经验生产比较。后续基于前沿的生产率和环境方法沿用同一生产逻辑。无论哪种方法，优化计算的含义都来自所提供的经济背景：谁对哪些数量负责、必须保留什么，以及哪些经营实践能够成为“可以做到什么”的可信证据。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:70
#: 5166784968ac4f649c1c89317400096d
msgid "Production possibilities and resource responsibility"
msgstr "生产可能性与资源责任"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:72
#: 1e11890266824bb19dffeea5a5901c72
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Let $x\\in\\mathbb{R}^m_+$ denote a vector of inputs and "
"$y\\in\\mathbb{R}^s_+$ a vector of desirable outputs. A production "
"technology is the set"
msgstr "以 $x\\in\\mathbb{R}^m_+$ 表示投入向量，以 $y\\in\\mathbb{R}^s_+$ 表示合意产出向量。生产技术是集合"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:75
#: bc381b0a09394582a4a7fea579ea4a8c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal{T}=\\{(x,y):x\\text{ can produce }y\\}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal{T}=\\{(x,y):x\\text{ 可生产 }y\\}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:79
#: 677b9995aa1f4db8af2e03215042b8bb
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Each element of $\\mathcal{T}$ is a feasible production plan. Economically, "
"$\\mathcal{T}$ describes the operating alternatives admitted by the study. "
"It is not a list of everything management could imagine, and it is not "
"identical to the rows that happened to be observed. The analyst builds it "
"from those observations using stated assumptions about comparability, "
"disposability, convexity, and scale. Its efficient boundary contains the "
"plans for which the available evidence supports no further improvement in at"
" least one relevant direction."
msgstr ""
"$\\mathcal{T}$ 中每个元素都是可行生产方案。从经济上说，$\\mathcal{T}$ "
"描述研究所允许的经营替代方案。它既不是管理者能够想象的一切方案清单，也不等于恰好观测到的数据行。分析者依据这些观测，并结合可比性、可处置性、凸性和规模的明确假设构造该集合。其有效边界由这样一些方案组成：在至少一个相关方向上，现有证据不再支持进一步改善。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:87
#: b3f09d29fd9b4a87b0da89b3879cfd18
msgid ""
"Consider a plant that uses 2 units of an aggregate resource to produce 1.5 "
"units of output. That record alone does not reveal whether resources are "
"well managed. It may be excellent performance under a demanding service "
"obligation or weak performance if comparable plants demonstrate that the "
"same output is attainable with less resource. Technical efficiency therefore"
" contains an empirical counterfactual: *what alternative plan is supported "
"by the study's production technology, for this organization and this "
"decision horizon?*"
msgstr ""
"设一家工厂使用 2 单位综合资源生产 1.5 "
"单位产出。仅凭这条记录，无法判断资源管理是否良好。在服务责任繁重时，它可能表现优异；如果可比工厂表明用更少资源也能实现同样产出，它也可能表现较弱。因此，技术效率包含一个经验反事实：*对于该组织和该决策期限，本研究的生产技术支持什么替代方案？*"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:95
#: 123476969790464b88a12bc44ab384da
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Koopmans called a feasible plan efficient when no other feasible plan can "
"use no more of every input and produce no less of every output, with a "
"strict improvement in at least one component {cite:p}`koopmans1951`. This "
"componentwise strong-efficiency criterion considers every input excess and "
"output shortfall. Debreu and Farrell developed scalar measures of common "
"proportional resource saving {cite:p}`debreu1951,farrell1957`. Related "
"Shephard distance functions supply the input- and output-oriented "
"representations used in modern production analysis "
"{cite:p}`shephard1953,fare1985`. Those contributions precede DEA and remain "
"essential for interpreting its scores."
msgstr ""
"Koopmans 把有效方案定义为：不存在另一项可行方案，在所有投入上都不多用、所有产出上都不少产，且至少有一项严格改善 "
"{cite:p}`koopmans1951`。这一逐分量的强有效准则考察每项投入冗余和产出不足。Debreu 与 "
"Farrell 发展了按共同尺度节约资源的标量测度 {cite:p}`debreu1951,farrell1957`；相关的 Shephard "
"距离函数则提供现代生产分析使用的投入导向与产出导向表示 {cite:p}`shephard1953,fare1985`。这些贡献早于 "
"DEA，至今仍是解释 DEA 得分的基础。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:105
#: ad21a7c391f446e7884e8a08a7473613
msgid "The distinction becomes concrete in a one-input, one-output example."
msgstr "在一个单投入、单产出的例子中，这一区别很直观。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 85c6733efd344ed6b786439c7207d8cf
msgid ""
"Eight production units, a VRS best-practice benchmark, and the resource-"
"saving and output-expansion targets of unit E"
msgstr "八个生产单元、VRS 最佳实践标杆，以及单元 E 的资源节约目标与产出扩张目标"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:112
#: e0839799e3ff45d08bd323428fb964d1
msgid ""
"An empirical variable-returns-to-scale benchmark. A--D represent best "
"observed practice under the maintained assumptions. For E, one comparison "
"asks how much input could be saved while preserving output; the other asks "
"how much output could be delivered with the current input."
msgstr ""
"一个经验规模报酬可变标杆。在既定假设下，A--D 代表最佳观测实践。对 "
"E，一项比较询问在保留产出的同时可以节约多少投入；另一项则询问用当前投入可以提供多少产出。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:118
#: 8b62e4207f3e44b798889cd0c4ce5034
msgid ""
"A--D supply the best-practice evidence for the variable-returns-to-scale "
"(VRS) technology in the figure. Read the two labelled comparisons as "
"different management questions. One holds E's output commitment fixed and "
"asks what resource budget would suffice. The other protects E's current "
"resource budget and asks what service level it could support. Neither "
"comparison says that management is free to choose both changes, or that the "
"indicated plan can be implemented without transition costs."
msgstr ""
"A--D 为图中的规模报酬可变（variable returns to "
"scale，VRS）技术提供最佳实践证据。两个标注的比较应理解为不同的管理问题：一项固定 E 的产出承诺，询问多大的资源预算已经足够；另一项保护 E "
"的当前资源预算，询问该预算能支持多高的服务水平。两者都没有表示管理者可以同时自由选择两种变化，也没有保证所示方案能在没有转型成本的情况下实施。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:125
#: b4974b4d11964eb48567d293f020ebf7
msgid ""
"The shaded region records plans treated as feasible under free disposability"
" of inputs and desirable outputs. The next two chapters examine who and what"
" may credibly be compared and then show how observations, convexity, "
"disposability, and returns to scale create this empirical opportunity set."
msgstr "阴影区域表示在投入与合意产出自由处置假设下视为可行的方案。接下来两章先审查哪些对象和数量可以可信比较，再说明观测、凸性、可处置性和规模报酬如何共同形成这一经验生产机会集合。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:130
#: 70b315ee846a4f1b9e2b55dbb4666d72
msgid ""
"Calling A--D “efficient” is conditional. It means that no feasible "
"comparison generated from this sample and these assumptions dominates them. "
"It does not establish that they use the best technology available outside "
"the sample, deliver the highest quality, or maximize social welfare. It also"
" does not make them universal role models: a peer is evidence under the "
"study's production model, not a verdict on every aspect of the organization."
msgstr ""
"称 A--"
"D“有效率”是有条件的：由本样本和这些假设生成的可行比较中，没有方案支配它们。这并不证明它们采用了样本外可得的最佳技术、提供了最高质量或实现了社会福利最大化，也不会使它们自动成为普遍榜样。活跃参照单元只是在本研究生产模型下提供证据，并不是对组织各方面的总体判决。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:137
#: 9b324553db254a4882741a15ccb8380d
msgid "What may management change?"
msgstr "管理者可以改变什么？"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:139
#: d4e236fbda504c57ac4d0f4348a93e6d
msgid ""
"Orientation turns organizational responsibility into a quantitative "
"question. Farrell's radial measures hold one side of production fixed while "
"changing the other proportionally. For an observed plan $(x_o,y_o)$, define "
"the input contraction factor and output expansion factor as"
msgstr ""
"导向把组织责任转化为数量问题。Farrell 径向测度保持生产的一侧不变，同时按比例调整另一侧。对于观测方案 "
"$(x_o,y_o)$，投入收缩因子和产出扩张因子定义为"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:144
#: 81c7c47b698e4b649e512e58ef28cc3c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\theta_o\n"
"  &=\\inf\\{\\theta>0:(\\theta x_o,y_o)\\in\\mathcal{T}\\},\\\\\n"
"\\phi_o\n"
"  &=\\sup\\{\\phi>0:(x_o,\\phi y_o)\\in\\mathcal{T}\\}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\theta_o\n"
"  &=\\inf\\{\\theta>0:(\\theta x_o,y_o)\\in\\mathcal{T}\\},\\\\\n"
"\\phi_o\n"
"  &=\\sup\\{\\phi>0:(x_o,\\phi y_o)\\in\\mathcal{T}\\}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:153
#: 6f9b8f16b5a84c8b86f22e8029a78bf5
msgid ""
"Under the standard monotonic technology, $0<\\theta_o\\leq1$ and "
"$\\phi_o\\geq1$. An input-oriented value of $\\theta_o=0.80$ says that the "
"represented technology supports a first-stage common reduction of 20 percent"
" in every input while outputs are preserved. An output-oriented value of "
"$\\phi_o=1.25$ says that a common 25 percent expansion of every output is "
"represented as attainable with the current inputs. To compare orientations "
"in a common higher-is-better display, this book also reports the reciprocal "
"$1/\\phi_o$. The expansion factor $\\phi_o$ retains the direct management "
"meaning; its reciprocal is only a bounded presentation."
msgstr ""
"在标准单调技术下，$0<\\theta_o\\leq1$ 且 $\\phi_o\\geq1$。投入导向值 $\\theta_o=0.80$ "
"表示：在保留产出的同时，被代表的技术支持第一阶段把每项投入共同减少 20%。产出导向值 $\\phi_o=1.25$ "
"表示：使用当前投入，把每项产出共同扩张 25% 被代表为可实现。为了在同一张“越高越好”的图中比较不同导向，本书也报告倒数 "
"$1/\\phi_o$。扩张因子 $\\phi_o$ 保留直接的管理含义；倒数只是有界的展示形式。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:162
#: 1b3ea95a898e43e49c2785bde919fde2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"For unit E in {numref}`fig-frontier-orientations`, the input-oriented "
"benchmark keeps the output commitment $y_E=1.5$ fixed and requires only "
"$4/3$ units of input. Hence"
msgstr ""
"对于 {numref}`fig-frontier-orientations` 中的单元 E，投入导向标杆固定产出承诺 $y_E=1.5$，只需 "
"$4/3$ 单位投入。因此"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:165
#: d821b14c6e374bf984f8c2b66488ad8e
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\theta_E=\\frac{4/3}{2}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\theta_E=\\frac{4/3}{2}=\\frac{2}{3}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:169
#: bb66a31846c14ee88e42685878007169
msgid ""
"The output-oriented benchmark instead treats $x_E=2$ as the available "
"resource budget and indicates an attainable output of $2.5$, giving"
msgstr "产出导向标杆改把 $x_E=2$ 视为可用资源预算，并表明产出 $2.5$ 可实现，从而得到"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:172
#: 4d76b3a9478041938a64b50e35ff9f8f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\phi_E=\\frac{2.5}{1.5}=\\frac{5}{3},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\phi_E}=0.6.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\phi_E=\\frac{2.5}{1.5}=\\frac{5}{3},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\frac{1}{\\phi_E}=0.6.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:178
#: d0d7cbd3a9c8466e99180f01c14bf2d9
msgid ""
"The two bounded efficiencies differ because they answer different management"
" questions. Input orientation is defensible when outputs are contractual or "
"policy commitments and the responsible manager can adjust resources. Output "
"orientation is defensible when the resource budget is fixed over the "
"relevant horizon and service or production can expand. A hospital may face "
"the first question in an annual budget review and the second during a short-"
"run access programme. Under VRS these counterfactuals need not identify the "
"same proportional performance gap. When neither describes the feasible "
"decision rights, a nonradial or directional measure may be more appropriate."
msgstr ""
"两个有界效率不同，是因为它们回答不同的管理问题。当产出是合同或政策承诺，而责任管理者可以调整资源时，投入导向较为合理；当相关期限内资源预算固定，而服务或生产可以扩张时，产出导向较为合理。医院在年度预算审查中可能面对前一问题，在短期可及性计划中则面对后一问题。在"
" VRS 下，这两个反事实不必给出相同的比例绩效差距。如果两者都不符合可行的决策权限，非径向或方向性测度可能更加合适。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:188
#: bc0cca4c1ac642b4ac18931b75695946
msgid ""
"A proportional benchmark also does not guarantee Pareto--Koopmans "
"efficiency. After the common percentage adjustment has been exhausted, a "
"particular resource may still be used in excess or a particular service may "
"remain below attainable practice. These variable-specific opportunities are "
"reported as slacks and motivate the additive, RAM, and slacks-based measures"
" developed later in the book. They should be read as benchmark evidence to "
"investigate, not automatic budgets or production quotas."
msgstr ""
"比例标杆也不保证 Pareto--Koopmans "
"有效。共同百分比调整已经用尽后，某项资源仍可能使用过多，或某项服务仍低于可实现实践。这些变量特定的机会以松弛量报告，并引出本书后续的加性、RAM "
"与基于松弛变量的测度。它们应被视为需要进一步调查的标杆证据，而不是自动形成的预算或生产配额。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:195
#: 6a1f2e7cad4a426698115e0b7a042683
msgid "Productivity level is a quantity account"
msgstr "生产率水平是一种数量核算"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:197
#: c5586f2fb5c84020bbb8e29a3f2cd56e
msgid ""
"With one input and one output, observed physical productivity can be written"
" as the ratio"
msgstr "在单投入、单产出情况下，观测实物生产率可以写成比率"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:200
#: 4c1d5b0e098c4914bda503e136e5907a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"AP_j=\\frac{y_j}{x_j}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"AP_j=\\frac{y_j}{x_j}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:204
#: e1fc8f3bed0d44168b94b64e342cee07
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"This average product is a property of the observed plan under an unambiguous"
" quantity ratio. It answers “how much output per unit of input?”, not “how "
"much improvement is supported by comparable practice?”. Technical efficiency"
" requires the latter benchmark comparison. In {numref}`fig-frontier-"
"orientations`, B has productivity $2.5/2=1.25$ and E has productivity "
"$1.5/2=0.75$. Under constant returns to scale (CRS), B's operating pattern "
"may be replicated proportionally, so E's radial efficiency happens to equal "
"the ratio $0.75/1.25=0.6$. That equality is a special one-input, one-output "
"CRS result, not a definition of technical efficiency."
msgstr ""
"该平均产出是在数量比含义明确时，观测方案自身的一项属性。它回答“每单位投入得到多少产出？”，而不是“可比实践支持多少改进？”。技术效率需要后一种标杆比较。在"
" {numref}`fig-frontier-orientations` 中，B 的生产率为 $2.5/2=1.25$，E 为 "
"$1.5/2=0.75$。在规模报酬不变（CRS）下，B 的经营方式可以按比例复制，所以 E 的径向效率恰好等于比率 "
"$0.75/1.25=0.6$。这是单投入、单产出 CRS 情形下的特殊结果，不是技术效率的定义。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:213
#: a085be34d59541d4a4f1cb37fc91f7a2
msgid ""
"Under VRS, A, C, and D can all represent best observed practice even though "
"their average productivities differ from B's. Each may use its represented "
"opportunities well at its own scale without operating at the scale that "
"delivers the largest output per unit of input. This is why a change from CRS"
" to VRS changes the benchmark and can separate technical performance at the "
"observed scale from scale performance; it does not alter the observed ratio "
"$y_j/x_j$."
msgstr ""
"在 VRS 下，A、C 和 D 的平均生产率即使不同于 "
"B，也都可以代表最佳观测实践。每个组织都可能在自身规模上充分利用被代表的机会，却未必处在单位投入产出最高的规模。这就是为什么从 CRS 改为 VRS "
"会改变标杆，并能把观测规模下的技术表现与规模表现分开；它不会改变观测比率 $y_j/x_j$。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:220
#: 8ba95f107138431480af6ab1f5c90567
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The distinction becomes more important with multiple inputs and outputs. "
"Nurse hours, bed-days, capital services, emergency visits, and elective "
"procedures cannot be added merely because they occupy adjacent spreadsheet "
"columns. There is no unique physical productivity ratio until quantities are"
" aggregated by an explicit quantity index. Such an index may use declared "
"quantity weights, price information within a consistent index-number "
"formula, or production-based quantity comparisons "
"{cite:p}`caves1982,coelli2005`. The middle account in {numref}`fig-three-"
"performance-accounts` deliberately counts its two service types equally:"
msgstr ""
"存在多项投入和产出时，这一区别更为重要。护士工时、床日、资本服务、急诊就诊和择期手术，不能因为出现在相邻的电子表格列中就直接相加。在数量指数明确聚合这些数量之前，不存在唯一的实物生产率比率。这种指数可以采用预先声明的数量权重、在一致指数公式中使用价格信息，或采用基于生产技术的数量比较"
" {cite:p}`caves1982,coelli2005`。{numref}`fig-three-performance-accounts` "
"中间的核算有意对两种服务等权计数："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:230
#: add09748d4fb46b5bc3a8f117940997e
msgid ""
"\n"
"AP_j^{eq}\n"
"=\\frac{y_{j,\\mathrm{standard}}+y_{j,\\mathrm{premium}}}{x_j}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"AP_j^{eq}\n"
"=\\frac{y_{j,\\mathrm{standard}}+y_{j,\\mathrm{premium}}}{x_j}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:235
#: e92aa21ad8be4c19a5b3740f8ee9dd4d
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The superscript $eq$ records the equal-count rule. It gives $AP_A^{eq}=2$ "
"and $AP_B^{eq}=1.8$. The account is transparent and useful for the teaching "
"comparison, but it is not a unique multi-output productivity measure "
"supplied by DEA. A different defensible aggregation rule could reverse the "
"ordering. A policymaker who values premium and standard service differently "
"is not correcting the DEA score; that person is defining a different "
"productivity or value account."
msgstr ""
"上标 $eq$ 记录等权计数规则；由此得到 $AP_A^{eq}=2$、$AP_B^{eq}=1.8$。这一核算透明，适合教学比较，但不是 DEA "
"自动提供的唯一多产出生产率测度。另一套同样合理的聚合规则可能颠倒次序。政策制定者如果赋予优质服务与普通服务不同价值，并不是在“纠正”DEA "
"得分，而是在界定另一种生产率或价值核算。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:242
#: cdec54470f184771befaae10b337c37c
msgid ""
"A productivity level also remains silent about *why* one organization has a "
"larger ratio. Case mix, operating scale, inherited capital, quality, and the"
" production opportunities available to different groups may all matter. It "
"is a descriptive quantity account until the study supplies an identification"
" strategy for a causal claim."
msgstr "生产率水平也不解释一个组织为何具有更高比率。病例组合、经营规模、继承资本、质量，以及不同群组可获得的生产机会都可能相关。在研究提供因果识别策略之前，它只是一种描述性数量核算。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:248
#: 7581d7c5351e412893b44638911c679b
msgid "Productivity change is a temporal account"
msgstr "生产率变化是一种时间核算"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:250
#: 1c31a35946d24ebe8b24e78455c3702c
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Across time, the question changes from “what is this period's output per "
"unit of input?” to “did aggregate output quantity change more favorably than"
" aggregate input quantity?”. Let $Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1}$ and $Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1}$ "
"denote declared output- and input-quantity indexes for organization $o$. One"
" complete multiplicative total-factor-productivity account is the Hicks--"
"Moorsteen index:"
msgstr ""
"跨期研究把问题从“本期每单位投入得到多少产出？”改为“总产出数量是否比总投入数量发生了更有利的变化？”。以 $Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1}$ 和 "
"$Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1}$ 表示组织 $o$ 已声明的产出与投入数量指数。一种完整的乘法全要素生产率核算是 Hicks--Moorsteen "
"指数："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:256
#: 94034c5adce740e6bbbe3daa8fe60a94
msgid ""
"\n"
"HM_o^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\frac{Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1}}{Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1}}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"HM_o^{t,t+1}\n"
"=\\frac{Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1}}{Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1}}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:261
#: 6cfb24a21abe4189b96ce06d54f581d6
msgid ""
"A value above one means that aggregate output quantity grew relative to "
"aggregate input quantity; one means no change; and a value below one means "
"decline. This statement requires stable organizational boundaries and "
"quantity definitions across the two periods. More patients recorded after a "
"coding change, or a lower labor input after contracted work is moved outside"
" the accounting boundary, is not automatically productivity growth."
msgstr ""
"大于 1 表示总产出数量相对于总投入数量增长；等于 1 表示不变；小于 1 "
"表示下降。要作出这种解释，两个时期必须具有稳定的组织边界和数量定义。如果患者数的增加来自编码变化，或劳动投入的下降只是因为把外包工作移出核算边界，就不能自动称为生产率增长。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:268
#: 82d842b8e27c4542ac63e55a373e319a
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Frontier-based measures use observed production possibilities to construct "
"the needed quantity comparisons. A Malmquist analysis may separate "
"productivity change into a change in how fully the organization used the "
"opportunities available in each period and a change in the best-practice "
"opportunities documented by the data "
"{cite:p}`fare1994,coelli2005,fried2008`. The first component is often called"
" *efficiency change* or *catch-up*. For management, it says whether the "
"operating shortfall relative to current peers narrowed or widened. It does "
"not establish that managers copied leaders, learned faster, or implemented a"
" particular reform. The second component says whether the best observed "
"resource--output possibilities became more or less favorable around the "
"organization's operating plans; by itself it is not a causal estimate of "
"innovation."
msgstr ""
"基于前沿的测度利用观测生产可能性构造所需数量比较。Malmquist "
"分析可以把生产率变化分为两部分：组织利用各期可得机会的充分程度发生了变化，以及数据所记录的最佳实践机会发生了变化 "
"{cite:p}`fare1994,coelli2005,fried2008`。第一部分通常称为*技术效率变化*或*追赶效应*。从管理角度看，它说明相对于当期活跃参照单元的经营不足是缩小还是扩大，却不能证明管理者复制了领先者、学习得更快或实施了某项改革。第二部分说明组织经营方案附近的最佳观测资源—产出机会变得更有利还是更不利；它本身并不是创新的因果估计。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:280
#: 18f64b5bc31c4a87995c7832355fc687
msgid ""
"Different mainstream productivity families use different scales. Malmquist "
"and Hicks--Moorsteen indexes are multiplicative and use one as the no-change"
" value. Luenberger indicators are additive and use zero. Their numbers "
"cannot be pooled into one ranking merely by labeling all of them "
"“productivity change”. Nor is a high static efficiency level the same as "
"productivity growth: an organization can remain close to best practice while"
" the represented technology contracts, or improve relative performance while"
" total productivity still falls."
msgstr ""
"不同主流生产率方法族采用不同尺度。Malmquist 与 Hicks--Moorsteen 指数是乘法对象，以 1 为无变化值；Luenberger "
"指标是加法对象，以 0 "
"为无变化值。不能仅因都贴上“生产率变化”标签，就把它们的数值混入同一个排名。较高的静态效率水平也不等于生产率增长：组织可以一直接近最佳实践，而被代表的技术却在收缩；也可以相对表现改善，但总生产率仍然下降。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:288
#: 095742d39eb0424a9ded1a689ed8b20a
msgid "Profitability and price recovery value the account"
msgstr "盈利能力与相对价格回收为数量核算赋值"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:290
#: f6af4a1e69904561a4bd1c2101530e66
msgid ""
"Quantity performance does not determine financial performance. Let $w_o$ "
"contain the input prices and $p_o$ the output prices applied to organization"
" $o$. For its observed plan $(x_o,y_o)$, define cost, revenue, profit, and "
"return-to-dollar profitability as"
msgstr ""
"数量绩效并不决定财务绩效。以 $w_o$ 表示适用于组织 $o$ 的投入价格，以 $p_o$ 表示产出价格。对于观测方案 "
"$(x_o,y_o)$，成本、收益、利润和投入一单位成本的回报率定义为"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:294
#: 7d12ed03358a498f8d1136bd5e848bc0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"C_o=w_o^\\top x_o,\\qquad\n"
"R_o=p_o^\\top y_o,\\qquad\n"
"\\Pi_o=R_o-C_o,\\qquad\n"
"\\rho_o^{RTD}=\\frac{R_o}{C_o}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"C_o=w_o^\\top x_o,\\qquad\n"
"R_o=p_o^\\top y_o,\\qquad\n"
"\\Pi_o=R_o-C_o,\\qquad\n"
"\\rho_o^{RTD}=\\frac{R_o}{C_o}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:301
#: 89a4342714a7413ea2cb055b3bad803d
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Profit is a monetary difference; $\\rho_o^{RTD}$ is return-to-dollar "
"profitability, or revenue per unit of expenditure. Neither is a technical-"
"efficiency score. A large organization can earn more total profit while "
"earning less revenue per dollar of expenditure, so profit and profitability "
"should not be used as synonyms. Both depend on the valuation system as well "
"as the physical production plan."
msgstr ""
"利润是货币差额；$\\rho_o^{RTD}$ "
"是投入一单位成本的回报率，即每单位支出的收益。两者都不是技术效率得分。大型组织可以获得更多总利润，却每单位支出获得较少收益，因此利润与盈利能力不能用作同义词。两者都取决于价值评价体系和实物生产方案。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:308
#: cadbee878f5842f69001d63ae3f0e5fd
msgid ""
"The distinction becomes especially important across time. Under an "
"internally consistent quantity--price index system, revenue and cost change "
"can be written as"
msgstr "跨期比较时，这一区别尤其重要。在内部一致的数量—价格指数体系下，收益与成本变化可以写成"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:311
#: a3e8d0082d6141a986b623ef1a9d422f
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\frac{R_o^{t+1}}{R_o^t}\n"
"=P_{y,o}^{t,t+1}Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\frac{C_o^{t+1}}{C_o^t}\n"
"=P_{x,o}^{t,t+1}Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1},\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\frac{R_o^{t+1}}{R_o^t}\n"
"=P_{y,o}^{t,t+1}Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1},\n"
"\\qquad\n"
"\\frac{C_o^{t+1}}{C_o^t}\n"
"=P_{x,o}^{t,t+1}Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1},\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:319
#: 15a365ef6b5d4d6088f505b5fbd3c9cf
msgid ""
"where $P_y$ and $P_x$ are output- and input-price indexes. It follows that "
"the change in return-to-dollar profitability has the accounting "
"decomposition"
msgstr "其中 $P_y$ 和 $P_x$ 分别为产出与投入价格指数。由此，每单位成本收益率的变化可按下式进行会计分解"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:322
#: d0a7cbe99c6f49dfb12983b6dbcd052a
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\frac{\\rho_o^{RTD,t+1}}{\\rho_o^{RTD,t}}\n"
"=\\underbrace{\\frac{Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1}}{Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1}}}_{\\text{productivity"
" change}}\n"
"\\underbrace{\\frac{P_{y,o}^{t,t+1}}{P_{x,o}^{t,t+1}}}_{\\text{relative-"
"price recovery}}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\frac{\\rho_o^{RTD,t+1}}{\\rho_o^{RTD,t}}\n"
"=\\underbrace{\\frac{Q_{y,o}^{t,t+1}}{Q_{x,o}^{t,t+1}}}_{\\text{生产率变化}}\n"
"\\underbrace{\\frac{P_{y,o}^{t,t+1}}{P_{x,o}^{t,t+1}}}_{\\text{相对价格回收}}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:328
#: f3b8b51f7d064d85ad311784b8122598
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Relative-price recovery asks whether output prices moved favorably compared "
"with input prices. It can improve while the organization's physical "
"quantities remain unchanged; productivity can improve while unfavorable "
"price movements reduce profitability. The decomposition is an accounting "
"identity only when the quantity and price indexes are constructed "
"consistently {cite:p}`odonnell2010profitability`. It does not say that "
"management caused a tariff change, wage settlement, exchange-rate movement, "
"or regulated reimbursement decision."
msgstr ""
"相对价格回收询问产出价格相对于投入价格是否发生了有利变化。即使组织的实物数量不变，它也可以改善；生产率也可能改善，却因不利的价格变化而使盈利能力下降。只有数量指数与价格指数按一致方式构造时，该分解才是会计恒等式"
" {cite:p}`odonnell2010profitability`。它不能说明管理者造成了收费标准变化、工资协议、汇率变动或受监管的补偿决定。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:336
#: cc136b36fdf24d3591748ba8f0bcd51f
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The four plans in {numref}`fig-three-performance-accounts` use one resource,"
" a standard service, and a premium service. At prices $w=2$ and $p=(3,5)$, A"
" earns $28/8=3.5$ units of revenue per unit of cost and a profit of 20. B "
"earns $37/10=3.7$ per unit of cost and a profit of 27. A nevertheless has "
"the greater equal-count physical throughput, while both A and B have input-"
"oriented VRS radial efficiency of one. Because this opening comparison does "
"not request slack completion, that score is not promoted to a Pareto--"
"Koopmans efficiency claim. This is the practical reason to keep the three "
"accounts separate."
msgstr ""
"{numref}`fig-three-performance-accounts` 中的四项方案使用一种资源、一种普通服务和一种优质服务。在价格 "
"$w=2$、$p=(3,5)$ 下，A 每单位成本获得 $28/8=3.5$ 单位收益，利润为 20；B 每单位成本获得 $37/10=3.7$，利润为"
" 27。尽管如此，A 的等权实物产出更高，而 A 与 B 的投入导向 VRS 径向效率都等于 "
"1。由于这一开篇比较并未要求完成松弛调整，该得分不会被提升为 Pareto--Koopmans 有效的结论。这正是实践中必须分开三种核算的原因。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:345
#: f92a94d404cd4bce8493cf967f640a26
msgid ""
"Observed prices also do not necessarily measure social value. A public "
"hospital's administered tariff, a utility's regulated price, or an emissions"
" permit price may be important for financial responsibility without "
"representing the full benefit or harm to society. Profitability, allocative "
"efficiency, and welfare therefore require their own declared valuation "
"questions."
msgstr "观测价格也不一定衡量社会价值。公立医院的行政收费、公用事业的受管制价格或排放许可价格，可能对财务责任很重要，却未必代表全部社会收益或损害。因此，盈利能力、配置效率和福利都需要各自明确的价值评价问题。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:351
#: ab5566d67dcf450fbd67672fa5506a18
msgid "Environmental performance keeps undesirable outcomes visible"
msgstr "环境绩效使非合意结果保持可见"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:353
#: 1c321a29c54e49aea91a886edd14aeb0
msgid ""
"Some organizations jointly produce services society wants and residuals it "
"wants to reduce. A power plant supplies electricity and emits carbon "
"dioxide; a hospital treats patients and may generate avoidable harm; a farm "
"produces food and nutrient runoff. Calling the residual an ordinary input "
"misstates its production role, while treating it as a desirable output "
"rewards more of it. The relevant technology records the joint account "
"explicitly:"
msgstr "有些组织在生产社会所需服务的同时，也产生社会希望减少的副产物。电厂供电并排放二氧化碳；医院诊治患者，也可能产生可避免伤害；农场生产粮食并造成养分径流。把这种副产物称为普通投入，会误述其生产角色；把它当作合意产出，则会奖励更多副产物。相关技术应明确记录联合核算："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:360
#: f2fb2f82e8b9430ea6d7f688872e0792
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T\n"
"=\\{(x,y,b):x\\text{ can jointly produce desirable output }y\n"
"\\text{ and undesirable output }b\\}.\n"
msgstr ""
"\n"
"\\mathcal T\n"
"=\\{(x,y,b):x\\text{ 可联合生产合意产出 }y\n"
"\\text{ 及非合意产出 }b\\}.\n"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:366
#: c8544f0384cf45eeb061e9f235aac530
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Environmental performance then asks what combination of useful-output "
"expansion, resource saving, and undesirable-output reduction is attainable "
"under this production account. The answer depends on the declared programme "
"and on assumptions about joint production and disposability "
"{cite:p}`murty2012`. A regulator asking a plant to maintain electricity "
"while reducing emissions poses a different question from a planner asking "
"how much electricity can expand while emissions and fuel are held fixed. "
"Directional and slacks-based environmental models later in the book make "
"those commitments explicit {cite:p}`chung1997,tone2003bad`."
msgstr ""
"环境绩效由此询问：在这种生产核算下，合意产出扩张、资源节约和非合意产出削减的什么组合可以实现。答案取决于预先声明的方案，以及联合生产与可处置性假设 "
"{cite:p}`murty2012`。监管者要求电厂维持发电量并减少排放，不同于规划者要求在固定排放和燃料时扩大发电量。后续的方向性和基于松弛变量的环境模型会明确这些承诺"
" {cite:p}`chung1997,tone2003bad`。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:376
#: 73d9a959e7214314aad60ce795c4b7bb
msgid ""
"Several tempting shortcuts answer other questions. Total emissions describe "
"a burden but ignore useful production; emissions per unit of output are an "
"intensity ratio but do not construct a multidimensional feasible "
"alternative. A technical-efficiency model that omits pollution can reward "
"resource saving while remaining silent about environmental performance. "
"Conversely, an environmental score does not attach a monetary damage to "
"emissions or establish social welfare. Across time, environmentally adjusted"
" productivity change requires a complete set of temporal comparisons; a "
"single cross-period environmental-efficiency value is not itself a "
"productivity index."
msgstr "几种看似方便的捷径实际回答了其他问题。排放总量描述负担，却忽略合意生产；单位产出排放是强度比，却不构造多维可行替代方案。遗漏污染的技术效率模型可以奖励资源节约，却对环境绩效保持沉默。反过来，环境得分不会为排放赋予货币损害，也不能确立社会福利。跨期的环境调整生产率变化需要一套完整的时间比较；单个跨期环境效率值本身不是生产率指数。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:386
#: ab5eee17e4cc40f3836ff15a248da385
msgid ""
"The five accounts can now be kept in their proper places. Technical "
"efficiency asks about represented operating opportunity. Productivity level "
"and change aggregate physical quantities, at one time and between times "
"respectively. Profitability and price recovery value those quantities. "
"Environmental performance changes the production account by retaining "
"undesirable outcomes. They can illuminate one another, but they do not share"
" a measurement scale and should not be collapsed into a universal "
"performance ranking."
msgstr "现在可以把五种核算各归其位。技术效率询问被代表的经营机会；生产率水平与变化分别聚合某一时点和跨时点的实物数量；盈利能力与相对价格回收对这些数量赋值；环境绩效则通过保留非合意结果改变生产核算。它们可以相互启发，却不共享同一测量尺度，不应合并为普遍绩效排名。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:394
#: 9add2d92282040e8a6c70c27ed70e13b
msgid "Reproducing the opening accounts with DEAPack"
msgstr "用 DEAPack 重现开篇核算"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:396
#: 765614cdd73141398ba050c467768b9b
msgid ""
"DEAPack can reproduce the comparison without treating endogenous DEA "
"multipliers as observed prices:"
msgstr "DEAPack 可以重现这些比较，而不会把 DEA 的内生乘数当作观测价格："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:432
#: af4b43c4035f4567b67b0cc91a7d9ba2
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The profitability model also compares each observed $\\rho_j^{RTD}$ with the"
" best return-to-dollar ratio available from the declared reference set. That"
" relative comparison is useful, but it does not convert profitability into "
"technical efficiency. Nor does a DEA multiplier chosen to support a "
"technical-efficiency score become a market price, a social value, or a "
"willingness to pay. The observed-price chapter returns to these distinctions"
" with cost, revenue, and profit objectives; the productivity chapters later "
"show what must remain stable for comparisons through time. The environmental"
" chapters use separate data roles and production assumptions because the "
"teaching dataset in this opening comparison contains no undesirable outcome."
msgstr ""
"盈利能力模型还会把每个观测 $\\rho_j^{RTD}$ "
"与已声明参考集中最佳的每单位成本收益率比较。这个相对比较很有用，但不会把盈利能力变成技术效率。为支持技术效率得分而选择的 DEA "
"乘数，也不会成为市场价格、社会价值或支付意愿。观测价格章将通过成本、收益与利润目标重新讨论这些区别；后续生产率章节说明跨期比较必须保持哪些内容稳定；环境章节使用不同的数据角色和生产假设，因为开篇教学数据没有非合意结果。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:442
#: 47fadf17f67547c6af1a0da7e8f62870
msgid "How DEA turns observed practice into comparative evidence"
msgstr "DEA 如何把观测实践转化为比较证据"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:444
#: 14f083f66df44170ae69b3ea2e3e16c9
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Farrell's central contribution was to measure productive performance "
"relative to an attainable standard rather than infer it from one average-"
"product ratio {cite:p}`farrell1957`. The original CCR formulation made that "
"comparison operational for organizations using several inputs to produce "
"several outputs {cite:p}`charnes1978`. Banker, Charnes, and Cooper then "
"introduced the VRS technology, allowing performance at the organization's "
"observed scale to be distinguished from the additional question of scale "
"performance {cite:p}`banker1984`."
msgstr ""
"Farrell 的核心贡献，是相对于可实现标准测量生产绩效，而不是从一个平均产出比中推断绩效 {cite:p}`farrell1957`。最初的 CCR"
" 模型使多投入、多产出组织可以实际开展这种比较 {cite:p}`charnes1978`。Banker、Charnes 与 Cooper 随后引入 "
"VRS 技术，使观测规模下的绩效能够与规模绩效这一附加问题区分 {cite:p}`banker1984`。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:452
#: 6ba3f73b8a184320880725c09ce54e44
msgid ""
"“Nonparametric” does not mean assumption-free. A DEA estimate depends on the"
" units in the reference sample, their comparability, the selected variables,"
" disposability, convexity, returns to scale, orientation, and any weight or "
"assurance-region restrictions. DEA avoids specifying a smooth functional "
"form such as Cobb--Douglas, but it replaces that choice with an explicit set"
" of production assumptions. Those assumptions state which observed practices"
" may count as evidence and how they may be combined. Changing them changes "
"the economic comparison, not merely a technical setting."
msgstr ""
"“非参数”并不等于“没有假设”。DEA 估计取决于参考集中的单元及其可比性、所选变量、可处置性、凸性、规模报酬、导向，以及任何权重或保证域限制。DEA "
"不需要指定 Cobb--Douglas "
"这类光滑函数形式，却以一组明确的生产假设取代这一选择。这些假设说明哪些观测实践可以作为证据，以及如何组合它们。改变假设会改变经济比较，而不仅是调整一项技术设置。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:461
#: f4300ef166544ebea68f601ac1e697e0
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The operating plans in {numref}`fig-frontier-orientations` are distributed "
"with DEAPack as the deterministic `frontier_1x1` dataset. The following "
"analysis reproduces three appraisals of E. Holding E's record fixed makes "
"the source of each difference visible: the first two change what the "
"organization is asked to adjust, while the third changes whether represented"
" operating patterns may be replicated proportionally across scale."
msgstr ""
"{numref}`fig-frontier-orientations` 中的经营方案随 DEAPack 以确定性 `frontier_1x1` "
"数据集发布。下面的分析重现对 E 的三项评价。固定 E "
"的记录，可以清楚看到差异来源：前两项改变组织被要求调整的数量，第三项则改变被代表的经营方式能否跨规模按比例复制。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 1ba114b6a55c4d6abfb1118367d86534
msgid "Management comparison"
msgstr "管理比较"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: d22a5a8afe284969becea2d4cad14114
msgid "Contraction or expansion factor"
msgstr "收缩或扩张因子"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 4a7226d8337045f3941f7e009cab3c94
msgid "Higher-is-better display"
msgstr "越高越好的展示值"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 694fa803b4f34dec82e41fa958f41198
msgid "VRS input-oriented"
msgstr "VRS 投入导向"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 86b7f13b9171464fbbc18617cc3f2dd1 883d434ca3f2402b98584b3ff2805382
msgid "0.6667"
msgstr "0.6667"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: d9432f997e3d4375bf43c6f372f3feb6
msgid "VRS output-oriented"
msgstr "VRS 产出导向"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 9016299d6fd545de8d6f239c61f2c68e
msgid "1.6667"
msgstr "1.6667"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 0dfee8ab138242f3bbade4680c11a39c 1ffe1af9243c46399f596d4d2cdf058c
#: 335ba589dfdf4383b2d268d998656ef4
msgid "0.6000"
msgstr "0.6000"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:107
#: 219bc5d242d94f61b4e5684a91d87605
msgid "CRS input-oriented"
msgstr "CRS 投入导向"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:506
#: ba1219a270fb46a8a1b4edaf1a43f897
msgid ""
"For the output-oriented appraisal, 1.6667 is the expansion factor $\\phi_E$ "
"and 0.6000 is its reciprocal. The shared value of 0.6000 in the last column "
"does not make the VRS output and CRS input comparisons the same question. "
"Under CRS, E's input target is 1.2 rather than the VRS target of $4/3$ "
"because proportional replication of the most productive activity is "
"admitted. Inspecting the associated targets turns each score into an "
"operating account:"
msgstr ""
"对于产出导向评价，1.6667 是扩张因子 $\\phi_E$，0.6000 是其倒数。最后一列共同出现 0.6000，并不表示 VRS 产出比较与 "
"CRS 投入比较回答同一个问题。在 CRS 下，E 的投入目标为 1.2，而非 VRS 目标 "
"$4/3$，因为模型允许按比例复制生产率最高的活动。查看相应目标方案，可以把每个得分还原成一项经营核算："

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:524
#: ce95a46bf12e4aaf85e150113e4e7102
msgid ""
"The target table should be read with the decision contract in view. It "
"records plans supported by the maintained technology, not forecasts of what "
"E will achieve or instructions that ignore adjustment cost, quality, and "
"institutional constraints. Later chapters add variable-specific excesses and"
" shortfalls, the organizations supporting a benchmark, and the components of"
" productivity change. Those quantities often carry more management "
"information than a rank based on the headline score."
msgstr ""
"阅读目标表时，必须牢记决策契约。表中记录的是既定技术所支持的方案，而不是 E "
"将会实现什么的预测，也不是忽略调整成本、质量与制度约束的命令。后续章节还会加入各变量特定的投入冗余与产出不足、支持标杆的组织，以及生产率变化的组成部分。这些数量往往比按主得分形成的排名包含更多管理信息。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:531
#: e426e3c83c8946eab20e67e5c9c21e02
msgid "What a performance statement can support"
msgstr "绩效陈述能够支持什么"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:533
#: a64091254f694738a0ed8c55252ea4d1
msgid ""
"A defensible technical-efficiency conclusion names its question and "
"benchmark. For this example, one may say that E's represented resource-use "
"efficiency is 0.667 when its output commitment is preserved, relative to the"
" eight observed units and the VRS, convex, freely disposable technology. "
"Saying only that “E is 66.7 percent efficient” discards the service "
"commitment, decision rights, comparison population, scale assumption, and "
"production account that define the estimand."
msgstr ""
"一项可辩护的技术效率结论必须说明问题与标杆。对于本例，可以说：在保留 E 的产出承诺时，相对于八个观测单元以及 VRS、凸且自由处置的技术，E "
"被代表的资源使用效率为 0.667。只说“E 的效率为 66.7%”，会丢掉界定目标量的服务承诺、决策权限、比较总体、规模假设和生产核算。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:540
#: 161a8c78abf34cdbb08a4b56f987fadb
msgid ""
"The corresponding claims for other accounts use different language. A "
"productivity level names the quantity aggregator. Productivity change names "
"both periods, the quantity index, and the reference-information policy. A "
"profitability result names the prices and distinguishes revenue per "
"expenditure from profit. An environmental result names the undesirable "
"outcome, joint-production and disposal assumptions, and the improvement "
"programme. None should borrow the percentage or rank of another account."
msgstr "其他核算的结论应采用不同语言。生产率水平要说明数量聚合器；生产率变化要说明两个时期、数量指数和参照信息政策；盈利能力结果要说明价格，并区分单位支出收益与利润；环境结果要说明非合意结果、联合生产与处置假设以及改进方案。任何一种核算都不应借用另一种核算的百分比或排名。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:547
#: b3ae274d80724bb4a92b74158636816d
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Comparability is especially important. Hospitals with different case "
"severity, teaching obligations, or emergency mandates may not share one "
"production technology even when their columns have the same labels. Adding "
"variables indiscriminately is not a remedy: with a fixed sample, a higher-"
"dimensional technology often places more units on sparsely supported parts "
"of the frontier. Protocols for DEA applications therefore treat DMU "
"definition, variable selection, isotonicity, sample size, and sensitivity "
"analysis as core modeling decisions {cite:p}`dyson2001`."
msgstr ""
"可比性尤其重要。即使数据列名称相同，病例严重程度、教学责任或急诊任务不同的医院也未必共享一项生产技术。不加区分地增加变量并不能解决问题：样本固定时，更高维的技术往往会让更多单元落在证据稀疏的前沿部分。因此，DEA"
" 应用规范把 DMU 定义、变量选择、单调性、样本规模和敏感性分析都视为核心建模决定 {cite:p}`dyson2001`。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:555
#: be2499f1bd7c4dad95b6af7ea9b2e170
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"Finally, numerical precision and empirical certainty are different. A score "
"may be calculated very accurately while the estimated opportunities remain "
"sensitive to sampling variation, measurement error, and outliers. Bootstrap "
"and robust-frontier methods address aspects of that uncertainty "
"{cite:p}`simar1998,daraio2007`; DEA scores alone do not identify causal "
"effects. More fundamentally, no statistical refinement can repair a "
"production account that assigns the wrong responsibilities, omits a binding "
"service commitment, or compares organizations that cannot credibly learn "
"from one another."
msgstr ""
"最后，数值精度不同于经验确定性。得分可以计算得非常精确，而估计的生产机会仍对抽样波动、测量误差和异常值敏感。Bootstrap "
"与稳健前沿方法处理这类不确定性的某些方面 {cite:p}`simar1998,daraio2007`；DEA "
"得分本身不识别因果效应。更根本的是，如果生产核算分配了错误责任、遗漏有约束力的服务承诺，或比较了无法可信相互学习的组织，任何统计修正都无济于事。"

#: ../../chapters/01-foundations/01-efficiency-productivity.md:564
#: 7b71dbd359f04c58858d518470295433
#, python-brace-format
msgid ""
"The next chapter asks which organizations and quantities belong in a "
"credible comparison. The chapter after it constructs the CRS and VRS "
"empirical technologies, showing how observed activities, convex "
"combinations, free disposability, and returns to scale turn a finite dataset"
" into the opportunity set used here. Part II then brings orientation and "
"scale together in the four classical radial formulations in "
